IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dog-act-domain`

-- =============================================================================
-- Dog Act 1976 (Western Australia) -- Part X, Miscellaneous
--
-- Isomorphic encoding of Division 1 s. 54 ("Regulations generally") and
-- Division 2 ss. 54A-54I ("Local government approvals": Subdivision 1
-- "Applications for approval" and Subdivision 2 "Objection and review
-- process"), as at the compilation dated 28 Nov 2024 [version 08-b0-00],
-- re-verified current 2026-09-09. Source lines 1721-1823 of
-- mrdoc_47983.txt. The shared s. 3 Penalty shape this file reads lives in
-- dog-act-domain.l4, imported above.
--
-- SCOPED OUT (cited at their site, never expanded -- both outside this
-- chunk's assigned line range, which begins at Part X / s. 54):
--   - s. 54(3) applies s. 50(1)-(3) (the general procedure for regulations,
--     itself keyed off s. 48 "Regulations to operate as local laws") to
--     regulations mentioned in s. 54. ss. 48 and 50 sit at source lines
--     1670 and 1697, before this chunk's line range starts (1721).
--
-- NOT drawn from, only overridden (no encoding needed): s. 54(2B) displaces
-- the default commencement rule in Interpretation Act 1984 s. 41(1)(b) for
-- a restricted-breed regulation; nothing is read FROM that section.
--
-- Administrative machinery with no fact a downstream rule would ever test
-- is recorded as inert prose rather than a force-fit predicate: s. 54(1)
-- (Governor's general regulation-making power), s. 54(2A) (power to
-- regulate a dangerous-dogs register) and s. 54(2C) (regulations may cover
-- the manner and timing of giving notices/information/documents).
--
-- One ambiguity found (full detail in the AMBIGUITY comment at its site
-- and in the returned ambiguities array): F-PRACTICABLE, s. 54B(1)'s
-- undefined "as soon as practicable" -- delegated to fact-supply, since
-- the Act states no numeric benchmark to derive one from.
-- =============================================================================

§ `Part X, Division 1 -- Regulations`
§§ `54. Regulations generally`

-- s 54(1): the Governor may make regulations for and in relation to any
-- matter the Governor thinks necessary or expedient for carrying this Act
-- into effect, including transitional/incidental/supplementary provisions.
-- Pure regulation-making power; no fact a downstream rule would test.

-- s 54(2A): without limiting (1), the Governor may make regulations for a
-- register of dangerous dogs. Same -- an empowering provision, not a fact.

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54(2B)
GIVEN `days since publication in the Gazette` IS A NUMBER,
      `days since the later day specified or provided for in the regulation` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a s 54(2B) restricted-breed regulation has come into operation` `days since publication in the Gazette` `days since the later day specified or provided for in the regulation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `days since the later day specified or provided for in the regulation`
    WHEN NOTHING                    THEN `days since publication in the Gazette` AT LEAST 7
    WHEN JUST `days since that day` THEN `days since that day` AT LEAST 0

-- s 54(2C): without limiting (1), regulations may (a) require or permit a
-- notice/information/document to be given in a certain way, including via
-- the centralised registration system or any other electronic means, and
-- (b) provide for when it is taken to have been given. This describes the
-- scope of a future regulation's content, not a fact this file can test --
-- the regulations themselves are not encoded here.

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54(2)
GIVEN `inconsistency exists between a regulation made under this Act and a local law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the regulation prevails over the inconsistent local law (s 54(2))` `inconsistency exists between a regulation made under this Act and a local law` MEANS
    `inconsistency exists between a regulation made under this Act and a local law`

-- s 54(3): applies s 50(1)-(3) (the general procedure for regulations
-- under s 48) to regulations mentioned in this section, in the same way.
-- s 48 and s 50 sit before this chunk's assigned line range (see header) --
-- scoped out, not expanded.

§ `Part X, Division 2, Subdivision 1 -- Applications for approval`
§§ `54A. Applications`

DECLARE `S54A Application` HAS
    `made in a manner and form approved by the CEO`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains the information prescribed`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `accompanied by the fee, if any, prescribed`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `complies with any other requirements that are prescribed`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54A(1)
GIVEN app IS A `S54A Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application satisfies the s 54A(1) requirements` app MEANS
        app's `made in a manner and form approved by the CEO`
    AND app's `contains the information prescribed`
    AND app's `accompanied by the fee, if any, prescribed`
    AND app's `complies with any other requirements that are prescribed`

DECLARE `S54A(2) Requirement` HAS
    `local government required the applicant to give further document or information, or to verify it by statutory declaration, within a specified time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applicant complied with the requirement within the specified time`                                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54A(2)-(3)
GIVEN r IS A `S54A(2) Requirement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the local government may refuse to consider the application (s 54A(3))` r MEANS
        r's `local government required the applicant to give further document or information, or to verify it by statutory declaration, within a specified time`
    AND NOT r's `applicant complied with the requirement within the specified time`

§§ `54B. Record of approval`

-- AMBIGUITY (F-PRACTICABLE): "as soon as practicable" (s 54B(1)) states no
-- fixed number of days -- unlike the day-count deadlines elsewhere in this
-- chunk (7 days in ss 54C/54E(2), 28/42/77/35 days in ss 54F/54H), there is
-- no number in the text to build a WITHIN or day-count predicate from.
-- Taken reading: delegate satisfaction of the "as soon as practicable"
-- standard to fact-supply, as a single BOOLEAN field. Rejected: inventing
-- a specific numeric benchmark (e.g. "within 7 days") the Act does not
-- state. See structured ambiguities array, entry F-PRACTICABLE.
DECLARE `S54B Record` HAS
    `decision to grant, refuse, renew or refuse to renew was entered in the centralised registration system, with the prescribed information, as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `updated to reflect any change notified under s 54C`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `updated to reflect any imposition or amendment of conditions on the approval`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `updated to reflect any expiry or cancellation of the approval`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `updated to reflect the outcome of any objection or review under s 54G or 54H`                       IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54B(1)-(2)
GIVEN r IS A `S54B Record`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the local government's record of the approval satisfies s 54B` r MEANS
        r's `decision to grant, refuse, renew or refuse to renew was entered in the centralised registration system, with the prescribed information, as soon as practicable`
    AND r's `updated to reflect any change notified under s 54C`
    AND r's `updated to reflect any imposition or amendment of conditions on the approval`
    AND r's `updated to reflect any expiry or cancellation of the approval`
    AND r's `updated to reflect the outcome of any objection or review under s 54G or 54H`

§§ `54C. Notice of change to information`

DECLARE `Part X Party` IS ONE OF
    `Approval Holder`
    `Local Government`
    `Objector`

DECLARE `Part X Action` IS ONE OF
    `give notice in writing of a change under s 54C`
    `give notice of a decision under s 54E`
    `lodge a written objection under s 54F`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54C
GIVEN `holder became aware of a change to information prescribed under s 54B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days since the holder became aware of the change` IS A NUMBER,
      `notice in writing of the change was given to the local government that granted the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54C offence -- holder fails to give notice of a change within 7 days` `holder became aware of a change to information prescribed under s 54B(1)` `days since the holder became aware of the change` `notice in writing of the change was given to the local government that granted the approval` MEANS
        `holder became aware of a change to information prescribed under s 54B(1)`
    AND `days since the holder became aware of the change` AT LEAST 7
    AND NOT `notice in writing of the change was given to the local government that granted the approval`

`s 54C penalty` MEANS
    Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 5_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54C
GIVEN `holder became aware of a change to information prescribed under s 54B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Part X Party` `Part X Action`
`s 54C notification duty` `holder became aware of a change to information prescribed under s 54B(1)` MEANS
    IF `holder became aware of a change to information prescribed under s 54B(1)`
    THEN PARTY `Approval Holder`
         MUST  `give notice in writing of a change under s 54C`
         WITHIN 7
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `Approval Holder`
               BECAUSE "notice in writing of the change was not given to the local government within 7 days, as s 54C requires"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `54D. Certificate and unique number to be given to holder of approval`

DECLARE `S54D(1) Facts` HAS
    `approval granted is a pet shop approval`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `certificate given to the person, containing the prescribed information`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `unique pet shop number issued to the person for the pet shop`            IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54D(1)
GIVEN f IS A `S54D(1) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the local government satisfies its s 54D(1) duties on granting an approval` f MEANS
        f's `certificate given to the person, containing the prescribed information`
    AND (   (NOT f's `approval granted is a pet shop approval`)
         OR f's `unique pet shop number issued to the person for the pet shop`)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54D(2)
GIVEN `certificate given to the person, containing the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the local government satisfies its s 54D(2) duty on renewing a pet shop approval` `certificate given to the person, containing the prescribed information` MEANS
    `certificate given to the person, containing the prescribed information`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54D(3)
GIVEN `the local government is satisfied the person's certificate has been stolen, lost, damaged or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the local government may give a replacement certificate under s 54D(3)` `the local government is satisfied the person's certificate has been stolen, lost, damaged or destroyed` MEANS
    `the local government is satisfied the person's certificate has been stolen, lost, damaged or destroyed`

§ `Part X, Division 2, Subdivision 2 -- Objection and review process`
§§ `54E. Notice of certain decisions made by local government`

DECLARE `S54E Decision` HAS
    `refusal to grant an approval to breed`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `refusal to grant or renew a pet shop approval`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `cancellation of an approval to breed or a pet shop approval, other than at the holder's own request` IS A BOOLEAN
    `imposition or amendment of conditions on an approval to breed or a pet shop approval`                IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54E(1)
GIVEN d IS A `S54E Decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54E applies to the decision` d MEANS
        d's `refusal to grant an approval to breed`
    OR  d's `refusal to grant or renew a pet shop approval`
    OR  d's `cancellation of an approval to breed or a pet shop approval, other than at the holder's own request`
    OR  d's `imposition or amendment of conditions on an approval to breed or a pet shop approval`

DECLARE `S54E Notice` HAS
    `states the decision`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `gives the reasons for the decision`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies the person's rights under ss 54F and 54H, being either to lodge a written objection with a subsequent right to apply to SAT, or to apply directly to SAT for review` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54E(2)(a)-(c)
GIVEN n IS A `S54E Notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 54E(2) notice satisfies its content requirements` n MEANS
        n's `states the decision`
    AND n's `gives the reasons for the decision`
    AND n's `specifies the person's rights under ss 54F and 54H, being either to lodge a written objection with a subsequent right to apply to SAT, or to apply directly to SAT for review`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54E(2)
GIVEN d IS A `S54E Decision`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Part X Party` `Part X Action`
`s 54E(2) notice duty` d MEANS
    IF `s 54E applies to the decision` d
    THEN PARTY `Local Government`
         MUST  `give notice of a decision under s 54E`
         WITHIN 7
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `Local Government`
               BECAUSE "written notice of the decision, its reasons and the objection/review rights was not given within 7 days, as s 54E(2) requires"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `54F. Objection may be lodged`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54F(1), (3)
GIVEN `the person has applied for a review of the decision under s 54H` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Part X Party` `Part X Action`
`s 54F(1) objection right` `the person has applied for a review of the decision under s 54H` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person has applied for a review of the decision under s 54H`
    THEN PARTY `Objector`
         MAY   `lodge a written objection under s 54F`
         WITHIN 28
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

DECLARE `S54F Objection` HAS
    `prepared in a form approved by the CEO`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains the information prescribed`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `lodged with the local government in a manner approved by the local government` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54F(2)
GIVEN o IS A `S54F Objection`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the objection satisfies the s 54F(2) requirements` o MEANS
        o's `prepared in a form approved by the CEO`
    AND o's `contains the information prescribed`
    AND o's `lodged with the local government in a manner approved by the local government`

§§ `54G. Dealing with objection`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54G(1)-(2)
GIVEN `objection is being dealt with by the council` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `objection is being dealt with by a committee authorised by the council to deal with the objection` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `that committee made the decision objected to` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the council made the decision objected to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the body handling the objection is properly constituted under s 54G(1)-(2)` `objection is being dealt with by the council` `objection is being dealt with by a committee authorised by the council to deal with the objection` `that committee made the decision objected to` `the council made the decision objected to` MEANS
        `objection is being dealt with by the council`
    OR  `a committee, unconflicted, is dealing with the objection`
    WHERE
        `a committee, unconflicted, is dealing with the objection` MEANS
                `objection is being dealt with by a committee authorised by the council to deal with the objection`
            AND NOT `a conflict exists`
        `a conflict exists` MEANS
            `that committee made the decision objected to` OR `the council made the decision objected to`

DECLARE `S54G Disposal` IS ONE OF
    `dismissing the objection`
    `varying the decision objected to`
    `revoking the decision objected to` HAS `another decision substituted` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `S54G Process` HAS
    `person who made the objection was given a reasonable opportunity to make submissions on how to dispose of the objection` IS A BOOLEAN
    `person who made the objection was given written notice of how the objection was disposed of, and the reasons for disposing of it in that way` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54G(3), (5)
GIVEN p IS A `S54G Process`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the objection was dealt with in accordance with s 54G(3) and (5)` p MEANS
        p's `person who made the objection was given a reasonable opportunity to make submissions on how to dispose of the objection`
    AND p's `person who made the objection was given written notice of how the objection was disposed of, and the reasons for disposing of it in that way`

§§ `54H. Review of decisions`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54H(1)
GIVEN `person lodged an objection to the decision under s 54F` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days elapsed since the objection was lodged` IS A NUMBER,
      `notice in writing of how the objection was disposed of has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may apply to SAT for review under s 54H(1)` `person lodged an objection to the decision under s 54F` `days elapsed since the objection was lodged` `notice in writing of how the objection was disposed of has been given` MEANS
        (NOT `person lodged an objection to the decision under s 54F`)
    OR  (    NOT `notice in writing of how the objection was disposed of has been given`
         AND `days elapsed since the objection was lodged` AT LEAST 35)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54H(2)
GIVEN `person lodged an objection to the decision under s 54F` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days since the person was given the s 54E notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `days since the objection was lodged` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application to SAT under s 54H(1) is made within time (s 54H(2))` `person lodged an objection to the decision under s 54F` `days since the person was given the s 54E notice` `days since the objection was lodged` MEANS
    IF `person lodged an objection to the decision under s 54F`
    THEN `days since the objection was lodged` GREATER THAN 35 AND `days since the objection was lodged` AT MOST 77
    ELSE `days since the person was given the s 54E notice` AT MOST 42

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54H(3)
GIVEN `days since the person was given notice of how the objection was disposed of` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application to SAT for review of the decision on the objection is made within time (s 54H(3))` `days since the person was given notice of how the objection was disposed of` MEANS
    `days since the person was given notice of how the objection was disposed of` AT MOST 42

§§ `54I. Suspension of effect of some decisions`

DECLARE `S54I Trigger` HAS
    `decision made to cancel an approval to breed or a pet shop approval, other than at the holder's own request`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `decision made not to renew a pet shop approval`                                                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `decision made under s 54G to dispose of an objection in a way resulting in the approval to breed or pet shop approval being cancelled`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `decision made under s 54G to dispose of an objection in a way resulting in a pet shop approval not being renewed`                        IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54I(1)
GIVEN t IS A `S54I Trigger`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 54I applies to the decision` t MEANS
        t's `decision made to cancel an approval to breed or a pet shop approval, other than at the holder's own request`
    OR  t's `decision made not to renew a pet shop approval`
    OR  t's `decision made under s 54G to dispose of an objection in a way resulting in the approval to breed or pet shop approval being cancelled`
    OR  t's `decision made under s 54G to dispose of an objection in a way resulting in a pet shop approval not being renewed`

-- s 54I(2)(b)'s "no longer any right to lodge an objection under s 54F or
-- apply to SAT under s 54H" is left as a single fact-supplied BOOLEAN
-- rather than re-derived from the s 54F/54H predicates above: doing so
-- would require threading the s 54E-notice clock, the s 54F objection
-- clock and the s 54H application clock all the way through this record,
-- for a fact this section only ever consumes as a yes/no gate. Not a
-- statutory ambiguity -- an encoding-economy choice, noted for the record.
DECLARE `S54I Status` HAS
    `an application has been made to SAT under s 54H for a review of the decision`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `SAT has determined that application`                                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is no longer any right to lodge an objection under s 54F or apply to SAT under s 54H in relation to the decision`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `SAT has ordered that the effect of the decision should not be suspended`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 54I(2)-(3)
GIVEN t IS A `S54I Trigger`, s IS A `S54I Status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the effect of the decision is suspended, and the approval continues to have effect, under s 54I` t s MEANS
        `s 54I applies to the decision` t
    AND NOT s's `SAT has ordered that the effect of the decision should not be suspended`
    AND (`review pending` OR `still within time to object or apply for review`)
    WHERE
        `review pending` MEANS
                s's `an application has been made to SAT under s 54H for a review of the decision`
            AND NOT s's `SAT has determined that application`
        `still within time to object or apply for review` MEANS
                (NOT s's `an application has been made to SAT under s 54H for a review of the decision`)
            AND NOT s's `there is no longer any right to lodge an objection under s 54F or apply to SAT under s 54H in relation to the decision`

-- =============================================================================
-- Illustrations
-- =============================================================================

§ `Illustrations`

§§ `54(2B) -- restricted-breed regulation commencement`

#ASSERT `a s 54(2B) restricted-breed regulation has come into operation` 7 NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 54(2B) restricted-breed regulation has come into operation` 6 NOTHING)
#ASSERT `a s 54(2B) restricted-breed regulation has come into operation` 2 (JUST 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 54(2B) restricted-breed regulation has come into operation` 2 (JUST -1))

§§ `54(2) -- priority of regulations over inconsistent local laws`

#ASSERT `the regulation prevails over the inconsistent local law (s 54(2))` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the regulation prevails over the inconsistent local law (s 54(2))` FALSE)

§§ `54A -- applications`

`a fully compliant application` MEANS `S54A Application` WITH
    `made in a manner and form approved by the CEO` IS TRUE
    , `contains the information prescribed` IS TRUE
    , `accompanied by the fee, if any, prescribed` IS TRUE
    , `complies with any other requirements that are prescribed` IS TRUE

`an application missing the prescribed fee` MEANS `S54A Application` WITH
    `made in a manner and form approved by the CEO` IS TRUE
    , `contains the information prescribed` IS TRUE
    , `accompanied by the fee, if any, prescribed` IS FALSE
    , `complies with any other requirements that are prescribed` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the application satisfies the s 54A(1) requirements` `a fully compliant application`
#ASSERT NOT (`the application satisfies the s 54A(1) requirements` `an application missing the prescribed fee`)

`a s 54A(2) requirement met on time` MEANS `S54A(2) Requirement` WITH
    `local government required the applicant to give further document or information, or to verify it by statutory declaration, within a specified time` IS TRUE
    , `applicant complied with the requirement within the specified time` IS TRUE

`a s 54A(2) requirement missed` MEANS `S54A(2) Requirement` WITH
    `local government required the applicant to give further document or information, or to verify it by statutory declaration, within a specified time` IS TRUE
    , `applicant complied with the requirement within the specified time` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`the local government may refuse to consider the application (s 54A(3))` `a s 54A(2) requirement met on time`)
#ASSERT `the local government may refuse to consider the application (s 54A(3))` `a s 54A(2) requirement missed`

§§ `54B -- record of approval`

`a s 54B record kept in full compliance` MEANS `S54B Record` WITH
    `decision to grant, refuse, renew or refuse to renew was entered in the centralised registration system, with the prescribed information, as soon as practicable` IS TRUE
    , `updated to reflect any change notified under s 54C` IS TRUE
    , `updated to reflect any imposition or amendment of conditions on the approval` IS TRUE
    , `updated to reflect any expiry or cancellation of the approval` IS TRUE
    , `updated to reflect the outcome of any objection or review under s 54G or 54H` IS TRUE

`a s 54B record that was never updated for a s 54C change` MEANS `S54B Record` WITH
    `decision to grant, refuse, renew or refuse to renew was entered in the centralised registration system, with the prescribed information, as soon as practicable` IS TRUE
    , `updated to reflect any change notified under s 54C` IS FALSE
    , `updated to reflect any imposition or amendment of conditions on the approval` IS TRUE
    , `updated to reflect any expiry or cancellation of the approval` IS TRUE
    , `updated to reflect the outcome of any objection or review under s 54G or 54H` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the local government's record of the approval satisfies s 54B` `a s 54B record kept in full compliance`
#ASSERT NOT (`the local government's record of the approval satisfies s 54B` `a s 54B record that was never updated for a s 54C change`)

§§ `54C -- notice of change to information`

#ASSERT `s 54C offence -- holder fails to give notice of a change within 7 days` TRUE 7 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 54C offence -- holder fails to give notice of a change within 7 days` TRUE 6 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 54C offence -- holder fails to give notice of a change within 7 days` TRUE 10 TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 54C penalty` EQUALS Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 5_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

#TRACE `s 54C notification duty` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Approval Holder` DOES `give notice in writing of a change under s 54C` AT 5
-- Result: FULFILLED (notice given within the 7-day window)

#TRACE `s 54C notification duty` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
-- Result: DEONTIC BREACHED -- no notice given within the 7-day window

§§ `54D -- certificate and unique number`

`a compliant breed-approval certificate` MEANS `S54D(1) Facts` WITH
    `approval granted is a pet shop approval` IS FALSE
    , `certificate given to the person, containing the prescribed information` IS TRUE
    , `unique pet shop number issued to the person for the pet shop` IS FALSE

`a compliant pet shop approval with its number issued` MEANS `S54D(1) Facts` WITH
    `approval granted is a pet shop approval` IS TRUE
    , `certificate given to the person, containing the prescribed information` IS TRUE
    , `unique pet shop number issued to the person for the pet shop` IS TRUE

`a pet shop approval missing its unique number` MEANS `S54D(1) Facts` WITH
    `approval granted is a pet shop approval` IS TRUE
    , `certificate given to the person, containing the prescribed information` IS TRUE
    , `unique pet shop number issued to the person for the pet shop` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the local government satisfies its s 54D(1) duties on granting an approval` `a compliant breed-approval certificate`
#ASSERT `the local government satisfies its s 54D(1) duties on granting an approval` `a compliant pet shop approval with its number issued`
#ASSERT NOT (`the local government satisfies its s 54D(1) duties on granting an approval` `a pet shop approval missing its unique number`)

#ASSERT `the local government satisfies its s 54D(2) duty on renewing a pet shop approval` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the local government satisfies its s 54D(2) duty on renewing a pet shop approval` FALSE)

#ASSERT `the local government may give a replacement certificate under s 54D(3)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the local government may give a replacement certificate under s 54D(3)` FALSE)

§§ `54E -- notice of certain decisions`

`a refusal to grant an approval to breed` MEANS `S54E Decision` WITH
    `refusal to grant an approval to breed` IS TRUE
    , `refusal to grant or renew a pet shop approval` IS FALSE
    , `cancellation of an approval to breed or a pet shop approval, other than at the holder's own request` IS FALSE
    , `imposition or amendment of conditions on an approval to breed or a pet shop approval` IS FALSE

`a cancellation at the holder's own request (s 54E does not apply)` MEANS `S54E Decision` WITH
    `refusal to grant an approval to breed` IS FALSE
    , `refusal to grant or renew a pet shop approval` IS FALSE
    , `cancellation of an approval to breed or a pet shop approval, other than at the holder's own request` IS FALSE
    , `imposition or amendment of conditions on an approval to breed or a pet shop approval` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 54E applies to the decision` `a refusal to grant an approval to breed`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 54E applies to the decision` `a cancellation at the holder's own request (s 54E does not apply)`)

`a fully compliant s 54E(2) notice` MEANS `S54E Notice` WITH
    `states the decision` IS TRUE
    , `gives the reasons for the decision` IS TRUE
    , `specifies the person's rights under ss 54F and 54H, being either to lodge a written objection with a subsequent right to apply to SAT, or to apply directly to SAT for review` IS TRUE

`a s 54E(2) notice silent on review rights` MEANS `S54E Notice` WITH
    `states the decision` IS TRUE
    , `gives the reasons for the decision` IS TRUE
    , `specifies the person's rights under ss 54F and 54H, being either to lodge a written objection with a subsequent right to apply to SAT, or to apply directly to SAT for review` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the s 54E(2) notice satisfies its content requirements` `a fully compliant s 54E(2) notice`
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 54E(2) notice satisfies its content requirements` `a s 54E(2) notice silent on review rights`)

#TRACE `s 54E(2) notice duty` `a refusal to grant an approval to breed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Local Government` DOES `give notice of a decision under s 54E` AT 6
-- Result: FULFILLED (notice given within the 7-day window)

#TRACE `s 54E(2) notice duty` `a refusal to grant an approval to breed` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
-- Result: DEONTIC BREACHED -- no notice given within the 7-day window

§§ `54F -- objection may be lodged`

#TRACE `s 54F(1) objection right` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Objector` DOES `lodge a written objection under s 54F` AT 20
-- Result: FULFILLED (objection lodged within the 28-day window)

#TRACE `s 54F(1) objection right` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 29)
-- Result: FULFILLED (MAY's benign omission -- no breach; standing right lapses unexercised)

`a fully compliant s 54F(2) objection` MEANS `S54F Objection` WITH
    `prepared in a form approved by the CEO` IS TRUE
    , `contains the information prescribed` IS TRUE
    , `lodged with the local government in a manner approved by the local government` IS TRUE

`a s 54F(2) objection lodged the wrong way` MEANS `S54F Objection` WITH
    `prepared in a form approved by the CEO` IS TRUE
    , `contains the information prescribed` IS TRUE
    , `lodged with the local government in a manner approved by the local government` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the objection satisfies the s 54F(2) requirements` `a fully compliant s 54F(2) objection`
#ASSERT NOT (`the objection satisfies the s 54F(2) requirements` `a s 54F(2) objection lodged the wrong way`)

§§ `54G -- dealing with objection`

#ASSERT `the body handling the objection is properly constituted under s 54G(1)-(2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the body handling the objection is properly constituted under s 54G(1)-(2)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the body handling the objection is properly constituted under s 54G(1)-(2)` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the body handling the objection is properly constituted under s 54G(1)-(2)` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)

`a fully compliant s 54G process` MEANS `S54G Process` WITH
    `person who made the objection was given a reasonable opportunity to make submissions on how to dispose of the objection` IS TRUE
    , `person who made the objection was given written notice of how the objection was disposed of, and the reasons for disposing of it in that way` IS TRUE

`a s 54G process with no notice of disposal` MEANS `S54G Process` WITH
    `person who made the objection was given a reasonable opportunity to make submissions on how to dispose of the objection` IS TRUE
    , `person who made the objection was given written notice of how the objection was disposed of, and the reasons for disposing of it in that way` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the objection was dealt with in accordance with s 54G(3) and (5)` `a fully compliant s 54G process`
#ASSERT NOT (`the objection was dealt with in accordance with s 54G(3) and (5)` `a s 54G process with no notice of disposal`)

`a dismissed objection` MEANS `dismissing the objection`
`a varied decision` MEANS `varying the decision objected to`
`a revocation with a substitute decision` MEANS `revoking the decision objected to` TRUE
`a revocation with no substitute decision` MEANS `revoking the decision objected to` FALSE

#ASSERT `a dismissed objection` EQUALS `dismissing the objection`
#ASSERT `a varied decision` EQUALS `varying the decision objected to`
#ASSERT `a revocation with a substitute decision` EQUALS `revoking the decision objected to` TRUE
#ASSERT `a revocation with no substitute decision` EQUALS `revoking the decision objected to` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a revocation with a substitute decision` EQUALS `a revocation with no substitute decision`)

§§ `54H -- review of decisions`

#ASSERT `the person may apply to SAT for review under s 54H(1)` FALSE 0 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person may apply to SAT for review under s 54H(1)` TRUE 10 FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person may apply to SAT for review under s 54H(1)` TRUE 35 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person may apply to SAT for review under s 54H(1)` TRUE 35 TRUE)

#ASSERT `the application to SAT under s 54H(1) is made within time (s 54H(2))` FALSE 42 0
#ASSERT NOT (`the application to SAT under s 54H(1) is made within time (s 54H(2))` FALSE 43 0)
#ASSERT `the application to SAT under s 54H(1) is made within time (s 54H(2))` TRUE 0 77
#ASSERT NOT (`the application to SAT under s 54H(1) is made within time (s 54H(2))` TRUE 0 35)
#ASSERT NOT (`the application to SAT under s 54H(1) is made within time (s 54H(2))` TRUE 0 78)

#ASSERT `the application to SAT for review of the decision on the objection is made within time (s 54H(3))` 42
#ASSERT NOT (`the application to SAT for review of the decision on the objection is made within time (s 54H(3))` 43)

§§ `54I -- suspension of effect of some decisions`

`a cancellation, not at the holder's request` MEANS `S54I Trigger` WITH
    `decision made to cancel an approval to breed or a pet shop approval, other than at the holder's own request` IS TRUE
    , `decision made not to renew a pet shop approval` IS FALSE
    , `decision made under s 54G to dispose of an objection in a way resulting in the approval to breed or pet shop approval being cancelled` IS FALSE
    , `decision made under s 54G to dispose of an objection in a way resulting in a pet shop approval not being renewed` IS FALSE

`no s 54I trigger present` MEANS `S54I Trigger` WITH
    `decision made to cancel an approval to breed or a pet shop approval, other than at the holder's own request` IS FALSE
    , `decision made not to renew a pet shop approval` IS FALSE
    , `decision made under s 54G to dispose of an objection in a way resulting in the approval to breed or pet shop approval being cancelled` IS FALSE
    , `decision made under s 54G to dispose of an objection in a way resulting in a pet shop approval not being renewed` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 54I applies to the decision` `a cancellation, not at the holder's request`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 54I applies to the decision` `no s 54I trigger present`)

`review pending at SAT, not yet determined` MEANS `S54I Status` WITH
    `an application has been made to SAT under s 54H for a review of the decision` IS TRUE
    , `SAT has determined that application` IS FALSE
    , `there is no longer any right to lodge an objection under s 54F or apply to SAT under s 54H in relation to the decision` IS FALSE
    , `SAT has ordered that the effect of the decision should not be suspended` IS FALSE

`SAT has already determined the review` MEANS `S54I Status` WITH
    `an application has been made to SAT under s 54H for a review of the decision` IS TRUE
    , `SAT has determined that application` IS TRUE
    , `there is no longer any right to lodge an objection under s 54F or apply to SAT under s 54H in relation to the decision` IS TRUE
    , `SAT has ordered that the effect of the decision should not be suspended` IS FALSE

`still within time to object, no SAT application yet` MEANS `S54I Status` WITH
    `an application has been made to SAT under s 54H for a review of the decision` IS FALSE
    , `SAT has determined that application` IS FALSE
    , `there is no longer any right to lodge an objection under s 54F or apply to SAT under s 54H in relation to the decision` IS FALSE
    , `SAT has ordered that the effect of the decision should not be suspended` IS FALSE

`all objection/review rights lapsed, no SAT application made` MEANS `S54I Status` WITH
    `an application has been made to SAT under s 54H for a review of the decision` IS FALSE
    , `SAT has determined that application` IS FALSE
    , `there is no longer any right to lodge an objection under s 54F or apply to SAT under s 54H in relation to the decision` IS TRUE
    , `SAT has ordered that the effect of the decision should not be suspended` IS FALSE

`SAT ordered no suspension, despite a pending review` MEANS `S54I Status` WITH
    `an application has been made to SAT under s 54H for a review of the decision` IS TRUE
    , `SAT has determined that application` IS FALSE
    , `there is no longer any right to lodge an objection under s 54F or apply to SAT under s 54H in relation to the decision` IS FALSE
    , `SAT has ordered that the effect of the decision should not be suspended` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the effect of the decision is suspended, and the approval continues to have effect, under s 54I` `a cancellation, not at the holder's request` `review pending at SAT, not yet determined`
#ASSERT NOT (`the effect of the decision is suspended, and the approval continues to have effect, under s 54I` `a cancellation, not at the holder's request` `SAT has already determined the review`)
#ASSERT `the effect of the decision is suspended, and the approval continues to have effect, under s 54I` `a cancellation, not at the holder's request` `still within time to object, no SAT application yet`
#ASSERT NOT (`the effect of the decision is suspended, and the approval continues to have effect, under s 54I` `a cancellation, not at the holder's request` `all objection/review rights lapsed, no SAT application made`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the effect of the decision is suspended, and the approval continues to have effect, under s 54I` `a cancellation, not at the holder's request` `SAT ordered no suspension, despite a pending review`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the effect of the decision is suspended, and the approval continues to have effect, under s 54I` `no s 54I trigger present` `review pending at SAT, not yet determined`)
